    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113216" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χᾰλυβδικός</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χᾰλῠβικός</span></b>  (later, acc. to St. Byz.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Chalybian,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίδηρος ὁ Χαλυβικός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mir.</u>
					833b22
				</span></i>
			: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χαλύβινος</span></b>  is
				v.l. in Sch. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				1259
			</span></i> cod.Laur.: ἡ
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
			</span></i>
			<i>the land of the Chalybes,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>of steel,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				247
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				1109
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄτερ Χαλυβδικοῦ</span> without
				<i>Chalybian,</i> i.e. without <i>steel,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				161
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χ. στόμωμα,</span>
			
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στόμωμα.</span>
			</div>
